---
// src/pages/disclaimer.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Educational & Non-Legal Advice Disclaimer | PrivacyLaw.free"
  description="Mandatory legal disclaimer: PrivacyLaw.free is an educational and informational research resource, not a legal advisory service."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-amber-950">
        Mandatory Notice
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Educational & Non-Legal Advice Disclaimer
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">
        Last updated: September 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-6 text-sm text-amber-950 leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Core Summary:</strong> PrivacyLaw.free is an independent educational platform created to make privacy law accessible to everyone for free. Content published on this website does not constitute formal legal advice, an attorney-client relationship, or a formal legal opinion.
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-slate mt-8 max-w-none text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. Not Legal Advice</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700">
          The materials and information on PrivacyLaw.free have been prepared for general informational and educational purposes only. They are not intended as legal advice, compliance counsel, or an endorsement of any particular business practice. You should not act or refrain from acting based on any content included on this site without seeking independent professional legal counsel licensed in your specific jurisdiction.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. No Attorney-Client Relationship</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700">
          Viewing this website, submitting inquiries, or interacting with any articles, tools, or links does not establish an attorney-client or fiduciary relationship between you and PrivacyLaw.free or any of its contributors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Factual Verification Standard</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700">
          We strive to maintain the highest standard of factual precision. Every case explainer is programmatically cross-verified against official regulatory decision records, binding board decisions, and court judgments using an automated deterministic verification pipeline. However, legal statutes evolve, appeals are lodged, and subsequent court interpretations may modify earlier decisions. We provide direct citations and links to official primary sources whenever available.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Certification & Study Preparation Notice</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700">
          References to certifications such as CIPP/E (Certified Information Privacy Professional/Europe), CIPM, CIPT, or AIGP (Artificial Intelligence Governance Professional) are for educational alignment and illustrative reference only. PrivacyLaw.free is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the International Association of Privacy Professionals (IAPP).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Strict Prohibition Against Automated Web Scraping & Data Extraction</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700">
          Automated bulk extraction, web scraping, robotic indexing (excluding compliant general web search engines obeying robots.txt), LLM dataset harvesting, or wholesale replication of PrivacyLaw.free content, structure, and editorial explanations is strictly prohibited without prior written authorization. Unauthorized scraping trips automated security defenses and violates our Terms of Use and international database protections.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

